    "body": "I agree the O(n²) cost of reading a whole witness with `btck_witness_stack_get_item_at` needs fixing. I'm less sure a new callback type is the best way to do it which #36909 is doing. Instead we could expose the witness's serialized bytes and let the bindings or caller decide how to decode them, this also follows the `*_to_bytes` functions we already have in the API.",
