      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Yuvicc, thanks for putting this up. It looks like it comes down to where the items are decoded. `btck_witness_stack_get_items` decodes them in the kernel and returns pointers that are valid for the duration of the existence of the witness stack and `btck_witness_stack_to_bytes` returns the serialization and each binding would decode the items themselves.\r\n\r\nWhat I'm trying to accomplish is to make an efficient form of the design that the API already has (`btck_witness_stack_get_item_at`) and to decode once in the kernel so that consumers don't need to reimplement consensus parsing.",
